  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 23 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D8"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the carboplatin shortage on 2023-04-28 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21, spanning 42 months.",
      "cites": ["E31", "D9"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Accord Healthcare product (NDC 16729-295-12) on the shortage list is manufactured by Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited (FEI 3004011473), a registered plant on the label.",
      "cites": ["E21", "E20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1191818 at that plant ended 2022-12-02 and was classified OAI, with the classification letter dated 2023-04-05 — 23 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E16", "D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An import alert (66-40) for Intas was published 2023-06-01, 34 days after the posting, and a warning letter was issued 2023-07-28, 91 days after the posting.",
      "cites": ["D5", "D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds two interchangeable carboplatin products: Teva (NDC 00703423901) and Apotex (NDC 60505628201), approved for substitution by P&T on 2026-05-16.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E32"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 18 days on hand (131 units at 7.3/day) and can spare 26 units while retaining a two-week buffer; Corvale Lakeside has 1.9 days on hand (4 units at 2.1/day) and would reach 14 days with the transfer.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3"]
    }
  ]
}
